Each muscle in the model was represented as a Hill-type muscle-tendon unit35 (Fig. 1). Muscle dynamics was described by two nonlinear, first order differential equations—activation and contraction dynamics—that relate the control—muscle excitation—to the states—muscle activation and either normalized fiber length or normalized tendon force. Activation dynamics was modeled based on Winters,27,33 using a tanh function to smoothly transition between activation and deactivation:1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
