T in series with a muscle with fiber length l
M, where the pennation angle α defines the angle between the tendon and the muscle fibers. Properties of muscle and tendon were described by dimensionless characteristics (Fig. 2). Five parameters scaled these generic characteristics for a specific muscle: optimal fiber length \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
